'''Alfred Joel Horford Reynoso''' {{post-nominals|post-noms=[[Order of Merit of Duarte, Sánchez and Mella|OMDSM]]}}<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |last=Group, 2006-2020 |first=Merit Designs Consulting |title=President Abinader awards Al Horford the National Order of Merit |url=https://dominicantoday.com/dr/people/2024/09/12/president-abinader-awards-al-horford-the-national-order-of-merit/ |access-date=2024-09-13 |website=DominicanToday |language=en}}</ref> (born June 3, 1986), nicknamed '''Big Al''', is a Dominican professional [[basketball]] player for the [[Golden State Warriors]] of the [[National Basketball Association]] (NBA). He is a five-time [[NBA All-Star]] and an [[NBA champion]].

Horford played [[college basketball]] for the [[Florida Gators men's basketball|Florida Gators]] and was the starting [[center (basketball)|center]] on their back-to-back [[National Collegiate Athletic Association]] (NCAA) national championship teams in [[2006 NCAA Division I men's basketball tournament|2006]] and [[2007 NCAA Division I men's basketball tournament|2007]]. He was drafted with the third overall pick in the [[2007 NBA draft]] by the [[Atlanta Hawks]], with whom he played nine seasons before signing with the Celtics as a free agent in the 2016 offseason.

After three seasons in Boston, Horford played for the [[Philadelphia 76ers]] and the [[Oklahoma City Thunder]] before being traded back to the Celtics prior to the 2021 season. He reached the [[NBA Finals]] with the Celtics in [[2022 NBA Finals|2022]] and [[2024 NBA Finals|2024]], winning his first NBA title in 2024.

